[Music]  Two and a Half Men was one of the  biggest hits in sitcom history but the  series finale was missing one of its  biggest stars for a very specific and  unique reason he didn't want to be  crushed to death by a piano so what did  Charlie Sheen want instead well to  understand the power struggle that led  to Sheen's absence from the series  finale first you have to understand the  decade of craziness that preceded it  when the show debuted on CBS in 2003 it  was an instant hit both Sheen and  co-star Jon Cryer were 80s icons  Reinventing themselves for a new  millennium and it worked Cryer told  Entertainment Weekly Charlie and I  really hit it off we had a great first  few years on that show it was incredibly  smooth we had a lovely time it was  working really well and then it suddenly  stopped working well as Sheen famously  and spectacularly went off the rails The  Tipping Point was reportedly Sheen's  2005 to force from Denise Richards  according to Cryer that's when Sheen  turned to drugs at first he could handle  it and he was still incredibly  professional and still Lovely by the way  to everybody on set but you could just  see that stuff was wearing on him it was  just the kind of trouble the show had  been hoping to avoid as Sheen had been a  tabloid regular in the 1990s Two and a  Half Men producer Chuck Laurie took a  chance on Sheen anyway writing the role  of Charlie Harper for Sheen but  following his divorce from Richards  Sheen began making headlines again for  all the wrong reasons he was accused of  hiring sex workers arrested on assault  charges and sentenced to rehab and anger  management among other things finally in  2011 during season 8 of Two and a Half  Men the show went on Hiatus so that  Sheen could deal with his problems  instead he refused to enter a facility  fired his private sobriety coach and  verbally attacked Laurie that was the  end Lori fired him and Sheen responded  with a typically unhinged statement  telling TMZ this is very good news they  continue to be in breach like so many  whales it is a big day of gladness at  the sober Valley Lodge because now I can  take all of the bazillions never have to  look at them again and I never have to  put on those silly shirts for as long as  this warlock exists in the terrestrial  Dimension Sheen wasn't exactly contrite  about his drug-fueled Antics in later  interviews either I don't know man I was  banging seven gram rocks and finishing  them because that's how I roll I have  one speed I have one gear go Two and a  Half Men survived Shin's departure by  killing off Charlie Harper and replacing  him with new character Walden Schmidt  played by Ashton Kutcher the show ran  several more seasons before ending in  2015 which is where the piano comes in  even though Charlie Harper was dead  producers hope to bring back Sheen for  the series finale the idea was that  Charlie would ring the doorbell then ran  to the camera about drug abuse and how  he was above all that then a piano would  fall from the sky killing him it would  be very meta and thus fit the humor of  the show however Sheen had something  totally different in mind he was willing  to appear in the finale but he wanted  his character's return to be a launching  pad for a proposed new spin-off series  called the Harpers which would have  reunited him with crier when the  producers didn't go for his idea he  refused to appear so instead The  Producers simply ran the scene anyway  only with a body double for the absent  Sheen and they added a coda where Lori  poked fun at both Sheen and himself as  well winning  it was weird end to Sheen's tenure on  Two and a Half Men but not the end of  his career or his personal growth in  2021 he told Yahoo entertainment that he  regretted how things went there was 55  different ways for me to handle that  situation and I chose number 56. and so  you know I think the growth for me post  meltdown or melt forward or melt  somewhere however you want to label it  it has to start with absolute ownership  of my role in all of it  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

